G907.b:
⟪βαπτίζω⟫
(< βάπτω), [in LXX: ⟦2 Kings 5:14|IV Ki 5:14⟧ (⁨טבל⁩), ⟦Isaiah 21:4|Is 21:4⟧, Jth 12:7, Si 31 (34):30*;] ⟪to dip⟫, ⟪immerse⟫, ⟪sink⟫;
⟪1.⟫ generally (in Polyb., iii, 72, of soldiers wading breast-deep; in i, 51, of the sinking of ships); metaph., ⟪to overwhelm⟫ (⟦Isaiah 21:4|Is 21:4⟧; cf. MM, Exp., x); c. cogn. acc., βάπτισμα β., ⟦Mark 10:38|Mk 10:38⟧, ⟦Mark 10:39|39⟧, ⟦Luke 12:50|Lk 12:50⟧. Mid.,
⟪2.⟫ ⟪to perform ablutions⟫, ⟪wash oneself⟫, ⟪bathe⟫ (⟦2 Kings 5:14|IV Ki 5:14⟧, Jth 12:7, Si 31 (34):30): ⟦Mark 7:4|Mk 7:4⟧; aor. pass, in same sense, ⟦Luke 11:38|Lk 11:38⟧.
⟪3⟫ Of ablution, immersion, as a religious rite, ⟪to baptize⟫;
	⟪(a)⟫ absol.; ⟦Mark 1:4|Mk 1:4⟧, ⟦John 1:25|Jo 1:25⟧, ⟦John 1:26|26⟧, ⟦John 1:28|28⟧ ⟦John 3:22|3:22⟧, ⟦John 3:23|23⟧, ⟦John 3:26|26⟧ ⟦John 4:2|4:2⟧ ⟦John 10:40|10:40⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:17|I Co 1:17⟧; ὁ βαπτίζων (= ὁ βαπτιστής, M, Pr., 127), ⟦Mark 6:14|Mk 6:14⟧, ⟦Mark 6:24|24⟧; c. acc., ⟦John 4:1|Jo 4:1⟧, ⟦Acts 8:38|Ac 8:38⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:14|I Co⟧ ⟦1 Corinthians 1:14|1:14⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:16|16⟧; c. cogn. acc., τὸ βάπτισμα, ⟦Acts 19:4|Ac 19:4⟧ (cf. ⟦Mark 10:38|Mk 10:38⟧, supr.); pass., ⟪to be baptized⟫, ⟪receive baptism⟫: ⟦Matthew 3:13|Mt 3:13⟧, ⟦Matthew 3:14|14⟧, ⟦Matthew 3:16|16⟧, ⟦Mark 16:16|Mk 16:16⟧, ⟦Luke 3:7|Lk 3:7⟧, ⟦Luke 3:12|12⟧, ⟦Luke 3:21|21⟧ ⟦Luke 7:29|7:29⟧ (τ. βάπτισμα) ⟦Luke 7:30|ib. 30⟧, ⟦Acts 2:41|Ac 2:41⟧ ⟦Acts 8:12|8:12⟧, ⟦Acts 8:13|13⟧, ⟦Acts 8:36|36⟧ ⟦Acts 9:18|9:18⟧ ⟦Acts 10:47|10:47⟧ ⟦Acts 16:15|16:15⟧, ⟦Acts 16:33|33⟧ ⟦Acts 18:8|18:8⟧; mid., ⟦Acts 22:16|22:16⟧ (M, Pr., 163);
	⟪(b)⟫ with prepositions: ἐν, of the element, ⟦Matthew 3:6|Mt 3:6⟧, ⟦Matthew 3:11|11⟧, ⟦Mark 1:4|Mk 1:4⟧, ⟦Mark 1:5|5⟧, ⟦Mark 1:8|8⟧, ⟦Luke 3:16|Lk 3:16⟧, ⟦John 1:26|Jo 1:26⟧, ⟦John 1:31|31⟧, ⟦John 1:33|33⟧ ⟦John 3:23|3:23⟧, ⟦Acts 1:5|Ac 1:5⟧ ⟦Acts 2:38|2:38⟧ ⟦Acts 10:48|10:48⟧ ⟦Acts 11:16|11:16⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 10:2|I Co 10:2⟧; εἰς, of the element, purpose or result (Lft., Notes, 155), ⟦Matthew 3:11|Mt 3:11⟧ ⟦Matthew 28:19|28:19⟧, ⟦Mark 1:9|Mk 1:9⟧, ⟦Acts 8:16|Ac 8:16⟧ ⟦Acts 19:3|19:3⟧, ⟦Acts 19:5|5⟧, ⟦Romans 6:3|Ro 6:3⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:13|I Co 1:13⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 1:15|15⟧ 10:2 ⟦1 Corinthians 12:13|12:13⟧, ⟦Galatians 3:27|Ga 3:27⟧; c. dat., ὕδατι, ⟦Luke 3:16|Lk 3:16⟧, ⟦Acts 1:5|Ac 1:5⟧ ⟦Acts 11:16|11:16⟧; ὑπὲρ τῶν νεκρῶν, perh. to fulfil the wish of a dead friend, ⟦1 Corinthians 15:29|I Co 15:29⟧ (v. ICC, in l.; cf. DB, i, 238 ff.; DCG, i, 169a; ii, 605b; Cremer, 126).†

G908.b:
*† ⟪βάπτισμα⟫, -τος, τό
(< βαπτίζω) , prop., the result of the act, τὸ βαπτίζειν, as distinct from βαπτισμός, the act itself, ⟪immersion⟫, ⟪baptism⟫;
⟪1.⟫ metaph., of affliction: ⟦Mark 10:38|Mk 10:38⟧, ⟦Mark 10:39|39⟧, ⟦Luke 12:50|Lk 12:50⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Of the religious rite of baptism;
	⟪(a)⟫ of John's baptism: ⟦Matthew 3:7|Mt 3:7⟧ ⟦Matthew 21:25|21:25⟧, ⟦Mark 11:30|Mk 11:30⟧, ⟦Luke 7:29|Lk 7:29⟧ ⟦Luke 20:4|20:4⟧, ⟦Acts 1:22|Ac 1:22⟧ ⟦Acts 10:37|10:37⟧ ⟦Acts 18:25|18:25⟧ ⟦Acts 19:3|19:3⟧; β. μετανοίας, ⟦Mark 1:4|Mk 1:4⟧, ⟦Luke 3:3|Lk 3:3⟧, ⟦Acts 13:24|Ac 13:24⟧ ⟦Acts 19:4|19:4⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ of Christian baptism; ⟦Romans 6:4|Ro 6:4⟧, ⟦Ephesians 4:5|Eph 4:5⟧, ⟦Colossians 2:12|Col 2:12⟧ (Tr., -μῷ, q.v.), ⟦1 Peter 3:21|I Pe 3:21⟧ (cf. Cremer, 130; Tr., Syn. § xcix).†

G922.b:
⟪βάρος⟫, -εος, τό,
[in LXX: ⟦Judges 18:21|Jg 18:21⟧ (⁨כּבד⁩), Jth 7:4, Si 13:2, II Mac 9:10, III Mac 5:47*;] ⟪weight⟫;
⟪(a)⟫ ⟪a weight⟫, ⟪burden⟫, lit. and metaph.: ⟦Matthew 20:12|Mt 20:12⟧, ⟦Acts 15:28|Ac 15:28⟧, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:17|II Co 4:17⟧, ⟦Revelation 2:24|Re 2:24⟧; ἀλλήλων τὰ β., ⟪one another's faults⟫, ⟦Galatians 6:2|Ga 6:2⟧; ἐν β., ⟪burdensome⟫: ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:6|I Th 2:6⟧, R, txt., but v. infr.;
⟪(b)⟫ in late Gk. (Soph., Lex., s.v.), ⟪dignity⟫, ⟪authority⟫: ἐν βάρει, ⟦1 Thessalonians 2:6|I Th 2:6⟧ (R, mg.; v. Milligan, ICG, in l.).†
SYN.: ὄγκος, an encumbrance; φορτίον, ⟪a burden⟫, that which is borne.

G973.b:
*† ⟪βιαστής⟫, -οῦ, ὁ (< βιάζω), late form of βιατάς;
⟪1.⟫ ⟪strong⟫, ⟪forceful⟫.
⟪2.⟫ ⟪violent⟫ (Philo): ⟦Matthew 11:12|Mt 11:12⟧ (v.s. βιάζω).†

G991.b:
⟪βλέπω⟫,
[in LXX chiefly for ⁨ראה⁩, also for ⁨פּנה⁩, etc. ;]
⟪1.⟫ of bodily sight;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to see, have sight⟫ (opp. to τυφλὸς εἶναι): ⟦Matthew 12:22|Mt 12:22⟧, ⟦John 9:7|Jo 9:7⟧, ⟦Acts 9:9|Ac 9:9⟧, ⟦Romans 11:8|Ro 11:8⟧, ⟦Revelation 3:18|Re 3:18⟧, al.;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to perceive, look (at), see⟫: absol., ⟦Acts 1:9|Ac 1:9⟧; c. acc., ⟦Matthew 7:3|Mt 7:3⟧, ⟦Mark 5:31|Mk 5:31⟧, ⟦Luke 6:41|Lk 6:41⟧, ⟦John 1:29|Jo 1:29⟧, al.; ὅραμα, ⟦Acts 12:9|Ac 12:9⟧; γυναῖκα, ⟦Matthew 5:28|Mt 5:28⟧; βιβλίον, ⟦Revelation 5:3|Re 5:3⟧, ⟦Revelation 5:4|4⟧; τ. βλεπόμενα, ⟦2 Corinthians 4:18|II Co 4:18⟧.
⟪2.⟫ Metaph., of mental vision;
	⟪(a)⟫ ⟪to see, perceive, discern⟫: absol., ⟦Matthew 13:13|Mt 13:13⟧, ⟦Luke 8:10|Lk 8:10⟧; δι’ ἐσόπτρου, ⟦1 Corinthians 13:12|I Co 13:12⟧; c. acc., ⟦Hebrews 2:9|He 2:9⟧ ⟦Hebrews 10:25|10:25⟧; seq. ὅτι, ⟦Hebrews 3:19|He 3:19⟧, ⟦James 2:22|Ja 2:22⟧;
	⟪(b)⟫ ⟪to consider, look to, take heed⟫: absol., ⟦Mark 13:23|Mk 13:23⟧, ⟦Mark 13:33|33⟧; c. acc., ⟦1 Corinthians 1:26|I Co 1:26⟧, al.; seq. πῶς, c. indic., ⟦Luke 8:18|Lk 8:18⟧, ⟦1 Corinthians 3:10|I Co 3:10⟧, ⟦Ephesians 5:15|Eph 5:15⟧; seq. τί, c. indic., ⟦Mark 4:24|Mk 4:24⟧; seq. εἰς πρόσωπον, of partiality, ⟦Matthew 22:16|Mt 22:16⟧, ⟦Mark 12:14|Mk 12:14⟧. Colloq. (for ex. from π., V. Deiss., LAE, 122; M, Pr., 107; MM, Exp., x; Milligan, NTD, 50), β. ἑαυτόν: ⟦Mark 13:9|Mk 13:9⟧; seq. ἵνα μή, ⟦2 John 1:8|II Jo 8⟧; β. ἀπό, ⟦Mark 8:15|Mk 8:15⟧ ⟦Mark 12:38|12:38⟧; seq. μή (cl. ὁρᾶν), c. fut. indic., ⟦Colossians 2:8|Col 2:8⟧, ⟦Hebrews 3:12|He 3:12⟧; id. c. aor. subj., ⟦Matthew 24:4|Mt 24:4⟧, ⟦Mark 13:5|Mk 13:5⟧.
⟪3.⟫ Of situation and direction (Lat. specto), ⟪to look, face⟫ (towards), places, etc. (seq. πρός, Xen, Hell., vii, 1, 17; ⟦Ezekiel 40:23|Ez 40:23⟧, 24): seq. κατά, c. acc., ⟦Acts 27:12|Ac 27:12⟧ (cf. ἀνα-, ἀπο-, δια-, ἐμ-, ἐπι-, περ-, προ-βλέπω), v. DCG, i, 446; ii, 596.
